---

The HUD's guest mascots (ui/Sources/SwarmHUD/MascotSheets.swift, built by ui/Tools/mascots.py)
are pixel art from these projects. Each one shows its credit in the open usage card.

- Neko: art by Kenji Gotoh (NekoDA, 1989), whom Nobuyuki Sasaki asked in 1997; the artist said
  the art is completely free to use. The sprite sheet is from oneko.js
  (https://github.com/adryd325/oneko.js), MIT, Copyright © 2022 adryd.
- Rubber duck, Ferris, Zappy, Snake, Cockatiel, Rocky (Marc Duiker), Panda (Jessie Ferris),
  Turtle (enkeefe), Snail (Kennet Shin), Chicken (Gulnur Baimukhambetova), Morph (Luís Santos),
  Rat (szlegp) and Deno (Jo Franchetti): from vscode-pets
  (https://github.com/tonybaloney/vscode-pets), MIT, Copyright (c) 2022 Anthony Shaw. Ferris the
  crab was designed by Karen Rustad Tölva (CC0).
- Go gopher: sprites by Egon Elbre (https://github.com/egonelbre/gophers), CC0. The Go gopher was
  designed by Renee French and is licensed under CC BY 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
- Office worker: from Pixel Agents (https://github.com/pablodelucca/pixel-agents), MIT, Copyright
  (c) 2026 Pablo De Lucca, based on JIK-A-4's MetroCity character pack (CC0).

